WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.040
All right. Today we're going to talk
about a product that you've probably

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.200
seen on the internet. It's called
ToneRight. It is a device for $200 that

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.639
you can get online. And what you're
supposed to do is put it on the bridge

00:00:10.639 --> 00:00:13.840
and it sends vibrations through the
musical instrument. This is designed for

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.640
newer instruments to basically bring the
tone out. Uh you have to convince the

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.519
wood that it's no longer a tree or a
piece of lumber, but something that is

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:27.840
designed to produce musical quality
tone. So, right here I have a fiddle,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.320
which is my great greatgrandfather's
from the 1890s. It's been played for a

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:38.399
long, long time. I play it every single
day. I have here a cheap Chinese

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:41.760
travel fiddle, if you will, something I
got off of Amazon and I've worked on to

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.039
modify. So, I'm going to show you what I
did. Instead of spending $200, which is

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:51.760
actually more than this thing cost, I'm
going to show you a hack and I really,

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.520
really think that it worked. All right,
so we've moved on to the dining room. I

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:01.600
have this heating mat and it has these
little vibrating modules inside of it so

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.000
you can do like a little back vibration
or whatever you want to do. Uh, but

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.760
instead of buying a $200 tone, I was
curious if this would work. And so I

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:16.080
took my fiddle
and I just basically placed it

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.479
bridge down.
Again, this is a crappy fiddle, so I

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:26.080
don't care. But I uh I did face down on
the little module and I just put it on

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:31.280
the low setting.
And you probably can't hear this from

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:36.079
the audio, but I can hear a lot of
vibration coming out of the actual

00:01:36.079 --> 00:01:41.600
interior of the fiddle.
And I have to be honest, after playing

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.159
this, after doing this for just even a
few hours, the fiddle sounded completely

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:52.960
different in a good way.
I think it works personally and I felt

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:59.640
like I noticed an immediate difference
in the quality of the instrument.
